description:
1.Senior Exterior designers must have in-depth knowledge of what it means to create great exterior designs which are on brand, and to an exceptional standard;
2.They must demonstrate a true understanding of the subtleties of 3D surface and translation of a 2D sketch into reality;
3.Main Tasks：Proposing innovative design solutions which help to push the future development of the Li Auto Brands;
4.Create compelling and appropriate design proposals for concept and production car programs in the form of sketches, renderings and 3D digital models.

1.Bachelors or higher degree in transportation / automotive design, industrial design;
2.Express a high level of creativity through sketching, digital sketching, and final digital rendering;
3.Skilled in Alias Automotive Studio, Photoshop and other visual Medias;
4.Ability to develop and maintain collaborative relationships with peers and colleagues across the organization, as well as internal clients;
5.Ability to work well autonomously and within a team in a fast-paced and deadline-oriented environment;
6.Strong aesthetic sensibilityFluent English communication skills.

About the team:
Our interior space team is one of the leading teams in industry, creating a cutting edge visionary experience for our future customers. With an exceptional focus on innovation and cutting-edge research, we have established ourselves as pioneers in the area of interior space design offering users an unforgettable immersive experience.
We welcome experts who are passionate about pushing the boundaries of Interior Design and are eager to contribute to our team's pioneering work. Join our team and be part of an exciting journey where you can help shape the world of the Li Auto Space Design, helping to be recognized globally for being at the forefront of innovation and technology, driving the interior Space experience forward.

Duties and responsibilities:
1. Lead the development of the vehicle's interior Space design with the mission of creating experiences for families that align seamlessly with our brand identity;
2. Help lead the design process and be involved in creating interior design solutions, from initial sketches to design models, and finally to manufacturing releases;
3. Collaborate with our 'Smart Space' and engineering teams to create exceptional and innovative forward thinking products;
4. Assume responsibility for establishing a design taste and working culture that harmonizes with our team in Beijing and Shanghai;
5. The function of this role is to help shape the future DNA of Li Auto products going forward. To help identify, define and develop future trends in automotive spaces and product sectors and instill them into our brands’ DNA. To be at the forefront of technology and innovation for the benefit of our users and help keep the company out in front as visionaries for products going forward.

Requirements:
Education/Experience
1. Bachelor degree or above, in industrial or transportation design;
2. Above 10 years’ experience in interior design, master of sketching, rendering and presentation skills;
3. Possess a solid theoretical foundation of interior car design from sketch to production, to be able to lead a design from first sketch until final tooling release;

Knowledge
1. Proficiency in using sketch and rendering software as well as general knowledge of modelling software;
2. Proficient English communication and writing skills, excellent team coordination and communication skills;

Skills and Competencies
1. Must have excellent negotiation and problem-solving skills;
2. Self-motivated & learning;
3. Proactive and creative.;
4. Excellent time management and ability to work under pressure;
5. Self-confidence. Self-motivated and goal driven. Orientation toward results.

1. Lead vehicle chassis tuning (e.g. kenimatics, air suspension, shock absorber, ARB, bushings, tires, EPS, ESP etc.) and chassis performance evaluations, developing luxury driving character;
2. Involve and ensure chassis and vehicle dynamics design fulfils the targets in digital simulation phase;
3. Lead and manage benchmark chassis performance evaluations including subjective and objective testing;
4. Define and align chassis performance targets. Develop respective measures together with relevant departments;
5. Improve chassis performance development procedure, chassis tuning process, chassis performance testing methods and standards;
6. Lead the development of CDC, EPS and other relevant chassis control calibration strategies;
7. Identify most harming and customer related parameters based on field researches, customer observation and feedbacks. Improve and optimize customer pain points;
8. Develop and integrate new chassis functions and technology for future productions;
9. R&H related issues finding and solving.

Education/Experience
1. Bachelor's, Master's or higher degree in mechanical engineering or automotive engineering or similar;
2. Over 15 years of experience in luxury brand vehicle subjective evaluation and chassis tuning;
3. Experienced in developing three or more luxury vehicles from concept to SOP;
4. Expert-level driving skills, subjective assessment skills and experience in extreme driving, able to take on guidance and training tasks;
5. Proficient with vehicle development process, especially regarding chassis development;
6. Experienced in air suspension tuning. Active suspension development or tuning experience is an advantage;
7. Highly experienced in target setting for chassis performance, and break down the target to system level requirement with the support of the CAE team;
8. Deep knowledge of chassis layout, hardpoint setting, parameters value and target setting.

Knowledge
1. Experienced with R&H simulation, measurement and chassis tuning software and tools;
2. Advanced MS Office skills in PowerPoint, Excel and Word;
3. Fluent English (oral and writing) is mandatory.

Skills and Competencies
1. Excellent collaboration and problem-solving skills;
2. Self-motivated, fast learning ability, proactive and creative;
3. Excellent time management and the capacity to work under pressure;
4. Strong self-confidence and results-oriented work philosophy;
5. Willing to travel to China (up to 20%).

1. Responsible for the overall architecture design and planning of the chassis by wire, and formulate technical routes and programs;
2. Work closely with hardware engineers and software engineers to design the electrical and electronic architecture, and develop control strategies and algorithms to realize the intelligent control of the chassis by wire system;
3. Conduct safety analysis based on chassis by wire functional architecture and definition, develop safety requirements at function level , and participate in the safety design of each function;
4. Be responsible for data collection and analysis during the testing process, timely detection and resolution of problems during testing, and optimization and improvement of the system;
5. Participate in fault diagnosis and troubleshooting of chassis by wire system, establish the FMEA system, and formulate the corresponding fault response measures;
6. Participate in the discussions of chassis by wire regulations or technical standards in Europe and globally, translate the content into system or safety design requirements, and into the software and hardware design of EMB. Represent Li Auto in the regulatory or technical standard discussions to propose suggestions or comments.

Education/Experience
1. 10 years+ experience in electric chassis system development, with mass production development experience and test verification experience in redundancy strategies and interaction design for EHB or EMB products;
2. At least more than 5 years experience, as a system leader or a key engineer, in electronic chassis system development in Tier 1 supplier, and have been working on redundant chassis systems, as a system leader or a key engineer, to support L3+ automatic driving systems.

Knowledge
1. Proficient in the architecture of wire-control chassis system, including the principle, structure and function of wire-control steering, wire-control braking, wire-control driving and other sub-systems, and familiar with the synergistic working mechanism among the sub-systems;
2. Be familiar with the basic principles of automotive dynamics and kinematics, and be able to apply the relevant theories to model and analyze the drive-by-wire chassis system;
3. Understand automotive electronic and electrical architecture, master CAN, LIN, FlexRay and other automotive communication protocols, as well as the working principle and application of related sensors and actuators;
4. Solid electronic chassis system development skills, proficient in the use of simulation software such as MATLAB/Simulink, AMESim, etc., capable of system-level modeling, simulation and optimization;
5. Proficiency in using system requirement tools, such as IBM DNG;
6. Fluent English (oral and writing) is mandatory.

Skills and Competencies
1. Excellent collaboration and problem-solving skills;
2. Self-motivated, fast learning ability, proactive and creative;
3. Excellent time management and the capacity to work under pressure;
4. Strong self-confidence and results-oriented work philosophy.

1. Responsible for the system requirement development and software architecture design of the full active suspension;
2. Responsible for the development and simulation validation of core control algorithms for the full active suspension, including body control and synergistic height adjustment control;
3. Responsible for the unit test of the developed software, as well as the preparation of related design and development documents;
4. Cooperate with chassis VD tuning engineers in parameter tunning and algorithm iterations, ensuring high quality overall performance delivery.

Education/Experience
10+ years of experience in suspension control field with excellency in automotive design theories and practices.

Knowledge
1. Proficiency in MBD for embedded systems and corresponding programming tools (Matlab/Simulink, C, Tasking, etc.) with a good programming style;
2. Strong background in modern and/or classical control theory, with good knowledge in MPC, LQ, ILC and other commonly used active suspension control algorithms;
3. Fluent English (oral and writing) is mandatory.

Skills and Competencies
1. Excellent collaboration and problem-solving skills;
2. Self-motivated, fast learning ability, proactive and creative;
3. Excellent time management and the capacity to work under pressure;
4. Strong self-confidence and results-oriented work philosophy.

1. Responsible for the technical development plan （system integration、system matching、function definition、etc.)，design guidebook，DFMEA and system standard preparation of the fully active suspension system;
2. Responsible for full active suspension system architecture and hardware sizing；
Includes active damper sizing and motor pump unit spec.design review；
Oil tube sizing and valves selection based on vehicle technical specification for full active suspension system function and NVH requirements;
3. Responsible for product definition of fully active suspension system and sub-components，proposing design requirements and standards for sub-components（such as fully active shock absorbers、motor pumps unit and oil Tube etc.), and collaborating with suppliers to optimize and design design schemes;
4. Responsible for developing DV & PV test projects，part verification，and problem tracking for fully active suspension；analyzing and solving bench test issues during development，vehicle-level assembly，performance，NVH，durability，and other issues;
5. Responsible for dynamic perception and technical exploration in the new technology field of fully active suspension; introducing new concepts，solutions，and technologies for innovative design and optimization of active suspension systems.

Education/Experience
1. Bachelor's, Master's or higher degree in mechanical engineering or automotive engineering or similar;
2. Over 10 years of experience in the field of fully active suspension systems;
3. Familiar with the principles of fully active suspension systems, including the design and development of fully active suspension systems, active shock absorbers, CDC solenoid valves, built-in accumulators, active hydraulic pumps and other components; able to independently complete the design, development and testing of fully active suspension systems to ensure that their performance/durability meets standards;
4. Master the characteristics and application scope of mainstream fully active system, possess the ability to reduce costs and improve performance, as well as the ability to analyze and solve problems, and provide technical support during product debugging and after-sales service.

Knowledge
1. Advanced skills in PowerPoint, Excel, Word and CATIA;
2. Sensitive to issue detection, root cause analysis and system performance evaluation;
3. Fluent English (oral and writing) is mandatory.

Skills and Competencies
1. Excellent collaboration and problem-solving skills;
2. Self-motivated, fast learning ability, proactive and creative;
3. Excellent time management and the capacity to work under pressure;
4. Strong self-confidence and results-oriented work philosophy.

1. Engineering Thermal Problem Solving
-Lead the investigation, analysis and solution of practical engineering thermal issues related to thermal management of core products such as electric drive systems, electronic motor, power electronic devices and power semiconductor devices；
-Form implementable engineering rectification plans and promote closed-loop verification to ensure the thermal safety and reliability of products under full working conditions.
2. Thermal Design and Simulation Optimization
-Take the lead in thermal design work of electric drive, power electronics and power semiconductors, formulate thermal design specifications and technical standards;
-Use CFD simulation tools to conduct steady-state/transient temperature field and flow field simulation, carry out multi-physics coupling simulation analysis, optimize heat dissipation schemes (air cooling, liquid cooling, phase change cooling, etc.), balance thermal performance, cost, space and manufacturability, and improve product thermal efficiency and power density.
3. Thermal Testing and Verification System Construction
-Lead the construction and upgrading of thermal testing platforms, formulate thermal test plans, test standards and DVP verification plans, organize product thermal performance tests, temperature rise tests, reliability tests, etc., analyze test data, revise simulation models, and improve simulation accuracy;
-Establish a thermal test database, accumulate test experience and technical parameters, and support product iteration and optimization.
4. Technical Capability Development
-Track the global technical development trends, industry standards and competitor dynamics in the Thermal field (electric drive, power electronics, power semiconductor direction);
-Take the lead in building the company's Thermal technology system, formulate the development plan of thermal management technology, promote the innovation of thermal management technology and the pre-research and implementation of cutting-edge technologies (such as new heat dissipation materials, advanced cooling schemes);
-Be responsible for the technical training and guidance of the team's Thermal technology, cultivate professional talents in thermal design and thermal simulation, and improve the overall technical capability of the team;
-Accumulate technical documents, design manuals and fault case databases, and promote the standardization of technology.

1. Education/Experience
-Master's degree or above, majoring in Engineering Thermophysics, Thermal Energy Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, Mechanical Engineering, Power Electronics and other related majors，PhD or 5+ years of experience at leading OEM or Tier-1/2 supplier preferred;
-Experience in industry-leading product development and mass production is preferred;
-Have successful experience in Edrive system, inverter, E-motor, OBC or power semiconductor development, and those who develop products to achieve mass production status are preferred.
2. Knowledge
-Proficient in the thermal characteristics and thermal management design principles of electric drive systems, power electronic devices and power semiconductor devices; proficient in various heat dissipation technologies such as air cooling, liquid cooling and phase change cooling; familiar with the selection and application of heat dissipation materials and heat dissipation components (radiators, liquid cooling plates, oil pumps, oil coolers, etc.);
-Familiar with relevant industry standards (such as automotive industry thermal management standards, power semiconductor thermal reliability standards, etc.); able to carry out thermal design and verification work in combination with standard requirements; understanding of ISO 26262 functional safety related requirements is preferred;
-Strong technical innovation capability; able to track cutting-edge thermal management technologies and carry out technical pre-research and implementation in combination with actual product needs; those with patents, technical papers and other achievements are preferred.
3. Skills and Competencies
-Passionate about engineering, with a strong spirit of innovation;
-Good team worker, strong sense of responsibility, good at communication especially work in different culture;
-Proficient iProficient in using at least one mainstream CFD simulation tool; familiar with 3D CAD software is preferred;
-Proactive, with pioneering spirit and a good sense of internal and external client;
-Good command of English written and oral communication skills.

1. Core Technology Leadership and Research
-Lead the mechanical design and integrated development of motors (stators, rotors, end covers, bearings and other core components);
-Formulate motor mechanical design specifications, technical standards and development processes；
-Take the lead in solving complex mechanical engineering problems (such as vibration and noise, structural strength, assembly accuracy, sealing reliability, etc.) in the process of motor R&D, production and application.
2. Technological Innovation and Cutting-Edge Technology Implementation
-Track the global technical development trends, industry standards and competitor dynamics in the motor mechanical field (motor structure, lightweight materials, precision manufacturing, assembly technology, etc.);
-Take the lead in carrying out pre-research on cutting-edge technologies (such as new motor structures, lightweight design, high-efficiency assembly schemes, etc.);
-Promote the transformation of technological innovation achievements into product applications, form core technology patents and technical barriers, and enhance the company's technical competitiveness.
3. Technical System and Capability Development
-Take the lead in building the company's motor mechanical technology system;
-Formulate technical development plans, improve technical documents such as motor mechanical design manuals, fault case databases and test standards, and promote the standardization of technology;
-Be responsible for team technical training, guidance and talent training, improve the team's overall motor mechanical design, technical research and engineering practice capabilities, and build a professional and efficient technical team.

1. Education/Experience
-Master's degree or above, major in Mechanical Design and Manufacturing and Automation, Mechanical Engineering, Vehicle Engineering, Power Machinery and Engineering and other related majors, PhD or 5+ years of experience at leading OEM or Tier-1/2 supplier preferred;
-Experience in industry-leading product development and mass production is preferred;
-Have successful experience in electric motor development, and those who develop products to achieve mass production status are preferred.
2. Knowledge
-Proficient in the mechanical design principles, structural optimization methods and manufacturing processes of motors (stators, rotors, end covers, bearings, etc.), proficient in core technologies such as motor structural strength, vibration and noise control, sealing design, and assembly accuracy control, and familiar with the selection and application of lightweight materials (aluminum alloy, composite materials, etc.);
-Familiar with the manufacturing processes of core motor mechanical components (such as machining, die casting, injection molding, welding, etc.), have good cost awareness and design for manufacturability capabilities, and be able to reduce motor product costs and improve production efficiency through design optimization;
-Familiar with relevant industry standards for motor mechanics (such as automotive industry motor mechanical design standards, motor structure design standards, etc.), have rich experience in motor product testing and verification, able to formulate test plans, analyze test data and promote closed-loop of test problems; those familiar with quality tools such as DFMEA and PFMEA are preferred.
3. Skills and Competencies
-Passionate about engineering, with a strong spirit of innovation;
-Good team worker, strong sense of responsibility, good at communication especially work in different culture;
-Proficient in using at least one mainstream 3D CAD design software and CAE simulation tools;
-Proactive, with pioneering spirit and a good sense of internal and external client;
-Good command of English written and oral communication skills.
